                    briefing_en: '<strong>Month 4 Results Are In</strong><br><br>A <strong>COP 15.4M cost overrun</strong> has been reported against the IC production budget. The CFO wants answers. Your task: decompose this variance into its three components.<br><br><strong>Data provided:</strong><br>- TiO2 pigment: paid COP 4,200/kg vs. standard COP 3,800/kg; purchased 8,400 kg<br>- Standard usage: 0.85 kg/unit x 38,000 units = 32,300 kg; actual = 34,100 kg<br>- Budgeted output: 40,000 units; actual: 38,000 units; fixed overhead/unit applied = COP 2,600<br><br>Additionally, a chemical distributor offers to supply SS-grade solvents at COP 67,000/unit (delivered). You must evaluate using relevant cost analysis.<br><br>Finally, set the transfer price for the Inmobiliaria Andina supply agreement for PA coatings.',
                    briefing_es: '<strong>Resultados del Mes 4</strong><br><br>Se ha reportado un <strong>sobrecosto de COP 15.4M</strong> contra el presupuesto de producción de IC. El CFO quiere respuestas. Tu tarea: descomponer esta variación en sus tres componentes.<br><br><strong>Datos proporcionados:</strong><br>- Pigmento TiO2: pagado COP 4,200/kg vs. estándar COP 3,800/kg; comprados 8,400 kg<br>- Uso estándar: 0.85 kg/unidad x 38,000 unidades = 32,300 kg; uso real = 34,100 kg<br>- Producción presupuestada: 40,000 unidades; real: 38,000 unidades; gasto fijo/unidad aplicado = COP 2,600<br><br>Adicionalmente, un distribuidor químico ofrece suministrar solventes grado SS a COP 67,000/unidad (entregado). Debes evaluar usando análisis de costos relevantes.<br><br>Finalmente, establece el precio de transferencia para el acuerdo con Inmobiliaria Andina para recubrimientos PA.',
                    controls: 'round2Controls',
                    dataPanel_en: '<table class="table table-sm"><thead><tr><th>Variance Component</th><th>Formula</th><th>Responsible Party</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Materials Price Variance</td><td>(Actual price - Standard price) x Actual qty purchased</td><td>Procurement</td></tr><tr><td>Materials Efficiency Variance</td><td>(Actual qty used - Standard qty allowed) x Standard price</td><td>Production</td></tr><tr><td>Volume Variance</td><td>(Budgeted units - Actual units) x Fixed overhead per unit</td><td>Demand / Sales</td></tr></tbody></table><br><table class="table table-sm"><thead><tr><th>SS Cost Category</th><th>Annual (M COP)</th><th>Avoidable?</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Direct materials</td><td>1,840</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>Direct labor</td><td>610</td><td>Yes (partially)</td></tr><tr><td>Variable overhead</td><td>930</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>Regulatory (40% avoidable)</td><td>280</td><td>Partial — 112</td></tr><tr><td>Factory fixed overhead</td><td>1,220</td><td>No — sunk</td></tr><tr><td>Depreciation</td><td>180</td><td>No — sunk</td></tr></tbody></table>',
                    dataPanel_es: '<table class="table table-sm"><thead><tr><th>Componente</th><th>Formula</th><th>Responsable</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Variación de Precio de Materiales</td><td>(Precio real - Precio estándar) x Cant. comprada</td><td>Compras</td></tr><tr><td>Variación de Eficiencia de Materiales</td><td>(Cant. usada - Cant. estándar permitida) x Precio estándar</td><td>Producción</td></tr><tr><td>Variación de Volumen</td><td>(Unidades presup. - Unidades reales) x Gasto fijo por unidad</td><td>Demanda / Ventas</td></tr></tbody></table><br><table class="table table-sm"><thead><tr><th>Categoría de Costo SS</th><th>Anual (M COP)</th><th>¿Evitable?</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Materiales directos</td><td>1,840</td><td>Sí</td></tr><tr><td>Mano de obra directa</td><td>610</td><td>Sí (parcialmente)</td></tr><tr><td>Gastos indirectos variables</td><td>930</td><td>Sí</td></tr><tr><td>Regulatorio (40% evitable)</td><td>280</td><td>Parcial — 112</td></tr><tr><td>Gastos fijos de fábrica</td><td>1,220</td><td>No — hundido</td></tr><tr><td>Depreciación</td><td>180</td><td>No — hundido</td></tr></tbody></table>'
                },
                {
                    title_en: 'Round 3 — Theory of Constraints and Capital Decision',
                    title_es: 'Ronda 3 — Teoría de Restricciones y Decisión de Capital',
                    briefing_en: '<strong>Constraint Identified: High-Speed Mixing Lines</strong><br><br>InduColora has 2 high-speed mixing lines running at <strong>100% utilization</strong>. These are the binding constraint on growth. Total mixing line capacity: 4,800 hours/year.<br><br><strong>Contribution margin (ABC) and mixing hours per unit:</strong><br>- PA: COP 17,100 CM, 2.8 hrs<br>- IC: COP 5,000 CM, 0.4 hrs<br>- SS: COP -16,100 CM, 3.2 hrs<br><br>A third mixing line is available for lease at COP 380M/year; it would add 2,400 mixing hours a year. Additionally, a client requests a custom specialty product: estimated CM of COP 22,000/unit requiring 1.6 mixing hours/unit.',
                    briefing_es: '<strong>Restricción Identificada: Líneas de Mezclado de Alta Velocidad</strong><br><br>InduColora tiene 2 líneas de mezclado de alta velocidad al <strong>100% de utilización</strong>. Son la restricción limitante para el crecimiento. Capacidad total: 4,800 horas/año.<br><br><strong>Margen de contribución (ABC) y horas de mezclado por unidad:</strong><br>- PA: MC COP 17.100, 2,8 h<br>- IC: MC COP 5.000, 0,4 h<br>- SS: MC COP -16.100, 3,2 h<br><br>Una tercera línea de mezclado está disponible por arrendamiento a COP 380M/año; agregaría 2.400 horas de mezclado al año. Adicionalmente, un cliente solicita un producto especial: MC estimada COP 22,000/unidad requiriendo 1.6 horas de mezclado/unidad.',
                    controls: 'round3Controls',
                    dataPanel_en: '<table class="table table-sm"><thead><tr><th>Product</th><th>CM/Unit (ABC)</th><th>Mixing Hours/Unit</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>IC</td><td>COP 5,000</td><td>0.4</td></tr><tr><td>PA</td><td>COP 17,100</td><td>2.8</td></tr><tr><td>Custom order</td><td>COP 22,000</td><td>1.6</td></tr><tr><td>SS</td><td class="costdec-sim-negative">COP -16,100</td><td>3.2</td></tr><tr><td>Third line (lease)</td><td>COP 380M/year</td><td>+2,400 h/year</td></tr></tbody></table>',
                    dataPanel_es: '<table class="table table-sm"><thead><tr><th>Producto</th><th>MC/Unidad (ABC)</th><th>Horas de mezclado/Unidad</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>IC</td><td>COP 5.000</td><td>0,4</td></tr><tr><td>PA</td><td>COP 17.100</td><td>2,8</td></tr><tr><td>Pedido especial</td><td>COP 22.000</td><td>1,6</td></tr><tr><td>SS</td><td class="costdec-sim-negative">COP -16.100</td><td>3,2</td></tr><tr><td>Tercera línea (arriendo)</td><td>COP 380M/año</td><td>+2.400 h/año</td></tr></tbody></table>'
                }
            ];
        }

        initialize(state) {
            if (this._brfTimer) { clearTimeout(this._brfTimer); this._brfTimer = null; }
            if (!state.domainState || Object.keys(state.domainState).length === 0) {
                state.domainState = {
                    revenue: 28400,
                    netMargin: 2.1,
                    netProfit: 596,
                    totalScore: 0,
                    cumulativeScore: 0,
                    marginHistory: [],
                    scoreHistory: [],
                    revenueHistory: [],
                    profitHistory: [],
                    ssActive: true,
                    r1Event: null,
                    r2Event: null,
                    r3Event: null
                };
            }
            if (!state.decisions || Object.keys(state.decisions).length === 0) {
                state.decisions = {
                    ssStrategy: 'maintain',
                    paPricing: 'maintain',
                    capacity: 'expandIC',
                    variancePrice: 0,
                    varianceEff: 0,
                    varianceVol: 0,
                    makeBuy: 'make',
                    transferPrice: 'market',
                    tocMix: 'optimize',
                    lease: 'lease',
                    customProduct: 'accept'
                };
            }
            // Undo rollback: the USF framework rewinds currentPeriod and re-calls initialize
            // but does NOT restore domainState. If state is ahead of the current period,
            // restore the entry snapshot for this period so KPIs/score/history roll back
            // correctly (persisted event rolls are kept for deterministic replay).  (v1.1.0)
            var __cp = state.currentPeriod || 1;
            var __ds = state.domainState;
            if (__ds._periodSnaps && __ds._periodSnaps[__cp] &&
                typeof __ds._snapPeriod === 'number' && __ds._snapPeriod > __cp) {
                var __rs = __ds._periodSnaps[__cp];
                Object.keys(__rs).forEach(function(k) { __ds[k] = JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(__rs[k])); });
                __ds._snapPeriod = __cp;
                __ds._periodSnap = JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(__rs));
                Object.keys(__ds._periodSnaps).forEach(function(k) { if (+k > __cp) delete __ds._periodSnaps[k]; });
            }
            this._bindLanguage();
            this._updateBriefing(state);
        }

        validateDecisions(decisions) {
            var round = (window.mySimulation.state.currentPeriod || 1);

            if (round === 1) {
                var ssEl = document.getElementById('ssStrategyInput');
                if (ssEl) decisions.ssStrategy = ssEl.value;
                var paEl = document.getElementById('paPricingInput');
                if (paEl) decisions.paPricing = paEl.value;
                var capEl = document.getElementById('capacityInput');
                if (capEl) decisions.capacity = capEl.value;
            } else if (round === 2) {
                var vpEl = document.getElementById('variancePriceInput');
                if (vpEl) decisions.variancePrice = parseFloat(vpEl.value) || 0;
                var veEl = document.getElementById('varianceEffInput');
                if (veEl) decisions.varianceEff = parseFloat(veEl.value) || 0;
                var vvEl = document.getElementById('varianceVolInput');
                if (vvEl) decisions.varianceVol = parseFloat(vvEl.value) || 0;
                var mbEl = document.getElementById('makeBuyInput');
                if (mbEl) decisions.makeBuy = mbEl.value;
                var tpEl = document.getElementById('transferPriceInput');
                if (tpEl) decisions.transferPrice = tpEl.value;

                var totalVar = decisions.variancePrice + decisions.varianceEff + decisions.varianceVol;
                if (Math.abs(totalVar - 15.4) > 0.5) {
                    window.mySimulation.uiManager.showNotification(
                        window.mySimulation.t('variance_sum_warning'), 'warning'
                    );
                    return false;
                }
            } else if (round === 3) {
                var tocEl = document.getElementById('tocMixInput');
                if (tocEl) decisions.tocMix = tocEl.value;
                var leaseEl = document.getElementById('leaseInput');
                if (leaseEl) decisions.lease = leaseEl.value;
                var cpEl = document.getElementById('customProductInput');
                if (cpEl) decisions.customProduct = cpEl.value;
            }

            return true;
        }

        calculateResults(state) {
            var ds = state.domainState;
            var round = state.currentPeriod;
            this._restoreEntry(ds, round);
            this._recordRound(state, round);
            var e = this._econ(ds, round);
            var sc = this._scores(ds, round, this._econ(ds, round, null, true));
            ds.revenue = Math.round(e.revenue);
            ds.netProfit = Math.round(e.profit);
            ds.netMargin = Math.round(10000 * e.profit / e.revenue) / 100;
            ds.totalScore = sc.overall;
            ds.cumulativeScore = sc.overall;
            ds.outcomeScore = sc.outcome;
            ds.processScore = sc.process;
            ds.performanceTier = this._tier(sc.overall);
            ds.performance = Object.assign({}, ds.performance || {}, { overallScore: sc.overall, outcome: sc.outcome, process: sc.process, tier: ds.performanceTier });
            ds.marginHistory[round - 1] = ds.netMargin;
            ds.scoreHistory[round - 1] = sc.overall;
            ds.revenueHistory[round - 1] = ds.revenue;
            ds.profitHistory[round - 1] = ds.netProfit;
            this._scheduleBriefing(state.currentPeriod + 1);
            this._showEvents(ds, round);
            return {
                period: round,
                roundScore: sc.overall,
                overallScore: sc.overall,
                score: sc.overall,
                outcomeScore: sc.outcome,
                processScore: sc.process,
                revenue: ds.revenue,
                netMargin: ds.netMargin,
                netProfit: ds.netProfit,
                cumulativeScore: sc.overall,
                eventKeys: this._eventKeys(ds, round)
            };
        }

        // Entry snapshot per period, so a resubmit or an undo recomputes from the same start (v1.1.0 idempotency kept)
        _restoreEntry(ds, round) {
            var keys = Object.keys(ds).filter(function (k) { return k.indexOf('_') !== 0; });
            if (ds._snapPeriod === round && ds._periodSnap) {
                var snap = ds._periodSnap;
                keys.forEach(function (k) { if (snap[k] !== undefined) ds[k] = JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(snap[k])); });
            } else {
                var sv = {};
                keys.forEach(function (k) { sv[k] = ds[k]; });
                ds._periodSnap = JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(sv));
                ds._snapPeriod = round;
                ds._periodSnaps = ds._periodSnaps || {};
                ds._periodSnaps[round] = JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(sv));
            }
        }

        // Decisions of this round stored by index, and the event rolls of this round drawn once and kept
        _recordRound(state, round) {
            var d = state.decisions || {}, ds = state.domainState;
            ds.dec = ds.dec || {};
            if (round === 1) ds.dec['1'] = { ssStrategy: d.ssStrategy, paPricing: d.paPricing, capacity: d.capacity };
            else if (round === 2) ds.dec['2'] = { variancePrice: +d.variancePrice || 0, varianceEff: +d.varianceEff || 0, varianceVol: +d.varianceVol || 0, makeBuy: d.makeBuy, transferPrice: d.transferPrice };
            else if (round === 3) ds.dec['3'] = { tocMix: d.tocMix, lease: d.lease, customProduct: d.customProduct };
            ds._rolls = ds._rolls || {};
            var roll = function (key, prob) { if (ds._rolls[key] === undefined) ds._rolls[key] = (Math.random() < prob); return ds._rolls[key]; };
            if (round === 1) roll('r1_ss', 0.30);
            if (round === 2) { roll('r2_tio2', 0.40); roll('r2_reg', 0.25); }
            if (round === 3) { roll('r3_comp', 0.20); roll('r3_div', 0.35); }
            ds.ssActive = !(ds.dec['1'] && ds.dec['1'].ssStrategy === 'drop');
        }

        /* The run-rate model, M COP per year, rebuilt from the decisions of rounds 1..r.
           Every figure comes from the briefing data: SS 79.4k units at COP 89,400, relevant cost 58,167,
           distributor offer 67,000, ABC full cost 105,500 (so 47,333 per unit is allocated cost that stays
           when the line goes), the 18k-unit internal PA supply at the three transfer prices, the variance
           data and the 2,400 hours a third mixing line adds at COP 12,500 of CM per hour. */
        _econ(ds, r, swap, expect) {
            var M = this.MODEL, D = ds.dec || {};
            var pick = function (rr, k, dflt) {
                if (swap && swap.round === rr && swap.key === k) return swap.value;
                var o = D[String(rr)] || {};
                return o[k] !== undefined ? o[k] : dflt;
            };
            var rolls = ds._rolls || {}, P = M.prob;
            var rv = function (k) { return expect ? P[k] : (rolls[k] ? 1 : 0); };
            var ss = pick(1, 'ssStrategy', 'maintain'), lost = rv('r1_ss');
            var rho = 1, price = M.ssPrice;
            if (ss === 'reprice') { rho = lost * M.rhoRepriceLost + (1 - lost) * M.rhoReprice; price = M.ssPrice * 1.4; }
            else if (ss === 'drop') rho = 0;
            else rho = lost * M.rhoLost + (1 - lost);
            var make = (ss === 'outsource') ? 0 : 1;
            if (r >= 2 && ss !== 'drop') {
                var mb = pick(2, 'makeBuy', 'make');
                make = mb === 'outsource' ? 0 : (mb === 'partial' ? 0.5 : 1);
            }
            var q = M.ssUnits * rho;
            if (r >= 3) q = q * (make + (1 - make) * M.requalKeep);
            var unitCost = make * M.ssRelevant + (1 - make) * M.ssOffer;
            var e = { profit: M.baseProfit, revenue: M.baseRevenue, parts: {} };
            var add = function (key, dp, dr) { e.parts[key] = (e.parts[key] || 0) + dp; e.profit += dp; e.revenue += (dr || 0); };
            add('ss', q * (price - unitCost) - M.ssUnits * (M.ssPrice - M.ssRelevant), q * price - M.ssUnits * M.ssPrice);
            if (ss === 'drop') e.stranded = M.ssUnits * M.ssStrandedUnit;
            if (r >= 2 && q > 0 && make > 0) add('reg', -M.regCost * make * rv('r2_reg'), 0);
            var pa = pick(1, 'paPricing', 'maintain');
            add('pa', pa === 'plus10' ? M.pa10 : (pa === 'plus18' ? M.pa18 : 0), pa === 'plus10' ? M.pa10Rev : (pa === 'plus18' ? M.pa18Rev : 0));
            var freed = Math.max(0, 1 - rho * make);
            var cap = pick(1, 'capacity', 'idle');
            if (cap === 'expandIC') add('cap', freed * M.capIC, freed * M.capICRev);
            else if (cap === 'newProduct') { if (r < 3) add('cap', -M.newProdCost, 0); else add('cap', freed * M.capNew, freed * M.capNewRev); }
            if (r >= 2) {
                var vp = +pick(2, 'variancePrice', 0) || 0, ve = +pick(2, 'varianceEff', 0) || 0;
                var aP = Math.max(0, 1 - Math.abs(vp - 3.36) / 3.36), aE = Math.max(0, 1 - Math.abs(ve - 6.84) / 6.84);
                var t2 = rv('r2_tio2');
                if (t2 > 0) { add('tio2', -M.tio2Cost * t2, -M.tio2Cost * t2); if (r >= 3 && aP >= 0.8) add('tio2', M.tio2Hedge * t2, M.tio2Hedge * t2); }
                var tp = pick(2, 'transferPrice', 'market');
                var TP = M.tp[tp] || M.tp.market;
                if (r === 2) add('tp', TP.r2, TP.r2Rev); else add('tp', TP.r3, TP.r3Rev);
                if (r >= 3) {
                    add('var', M.effSaving * aE + M.priceSaving * aP, 0);
                    if (ve > 6.84 + 1) add('var', -M.blameCost, 0);
                }
            }
            if (r >= 3) {
                var toc = pick(3, 'tocMix', 'statusQuo');
                if (toc === 'optimize') add('toc', M.tocOpt, M.tocOptRev);
                else if (toc === 'manual') add('toc', M.tocManual, M.tocManualRev);
                var c3 = rv('r3_comp');
                if (c3 > 0) add('comp', M.compExit * c3, M.compExitRev * c3);
                if (pick(3, 'lease', 'noLease') === 'lease') {
                    add('lease', M.leaseHours * M.icPerHour * (1 + 0.1 * c3) - M.leaseCost, M.leaseRev);
                    add('lease', -M.leaseCredit * rv('r3_div'), 0);
                }
                if (pick(3, 'customProduct', 'reject') === 'accept') add('custom', M.customCM, M.customRev);
            }
            return e;
        }

        _scores(ds, r, e) {
            var M = this.MODEL;
            var out = Math.max(0, Math.min(100, 100 * (e.profit - M.loProfit) / (M.hiProfit - M.loProfit)));
            var proc = null;
            if (r >= 2) {
                var d2 = (ds.dec || {})['2'] || {};
                var err = Math.abs((+d2.variancePrice || 0) - 3.36) + Math.abs((+d2.varianceEff || 0) - 6.84) + Math.abs((+d2.varianceVol || 0) - 5.20);
                proc = Math.max(0, Math.min(100, 100 * (1 - err / M.errZero)));
            }
            var comp = proc === null ? out : (1 - M.processWeight) * out + M.processWeight * proc;
            return { outcome: Math.round(out), process: proc === null ? null : Math.round(proc), overall: Math.max(0, Math.min(100, Math.round(comp))) };
        }

        _tier(score) {
            if (score >= 85) return 'excellent';
            if (score >= 70) return 'good';
            if (score >= 50) return 'developing';
            return 'beginner';
        }

        _eventKeys(ds, round) {
            var R = ds._rolls || {}, k = [];
            if (round === 1 && R.r1_ss && ds.ssActive) k.push('event_ss_customer');
            if (round === 2 && R.r2_tio2) k.push('event_tio2_spike');
            if (round === 2 && R.r2_reg && ds.ssActive) k.push('event_reg_change');
            if (round === 3 && R.r3_comp) k.push('event_competitor_exit');
            if (round === 3 && R.r3_div) k.push('event_dividend');
            return k;
        }

        _showEvents(ds, round) {
            var keys = this._eventKeys(ds, round);
            ds.lastEventKeys = keys;
            this._paintEvents(keys);
        }

        _paintEvents(keys) {
            var el = document.getElementById('eventAlert');
            if (!el) return;
            if (!keys || !keys.length) { el.style.display = 'none'; el.innerHTML = ''; return; }
            var self = this;
            el.innerHTML = keys.map(function (k) { return self._t(k); }).join('<br>');
            el.style.display = 'block';
        }

        _scheduleBriefing(nextP) {
            var self = this;
            if (this._brfTimer) clearTimeout(this._brfTimer);
            this._brfTimer = setTimeout(function () { self._updateBriefing({ currentPeriod: nextP }); }, 500);
        }

        setupUI(uiManager) {
            var self = this;
            uiManager.bind('currentDay', 'currentPeriod');
            uiManager.bind('maxPeriods', 'maxPeriods');
            uiManager.bind('revenueDisplay', 'domainState.revenue', function (v) { return self._fmt(v, 0); });
            uiManager.bind('netMarginDisplay', 'domainState.netMargin', function (v) { return self._fmt(v, 1) + '%'; });
            uiManager.bind('scoreDisplay', 'domainState.totalScore', function (v) { return String(Math.round(v)); });
            uiManager.bind('profitDisplay', 'domainState.netProfit', function (v) { return self._fmt(v, 0); });
        }

        getChartConfig() {
            return {
                marginChart: {
                    type: 'line',
                    data: {
                        labels: [],
                        datasets: [{
                            label: this._t('chart_margin'),
                            data: [],
                            borderColor: '#1e7e45',
                            backgroundColor: 'rgba(39,174,96,0.1)',
                            borderWidth: 3,
                            fill: false,
                            tension: 0.3
                        }, {
                            label: this._t('chart_revenue'),
                            data: [],
                            borderColor: '#2c5f8a',
                            backgroundColor: 'rgba(44,95,138,0.1)',
                            borderWidth: 3,
                            fill: false,
                            tension: 0.3,
                            yAxisID: 'y1'
                        }]
                    },
                    options: {
                        responsive: true,
                        maintainAspectRatio: false,
                        plugins: {
                            title: { display: true, text: this._t('chart_fin_title') }
                        },
                        scales: {
                            y: { beginAtZero: false, title: { display: true, text: this._t('chart_margin') } },
                            y1: { position: 'right', beginAtZero: false, title: { display: true, text: this._t('chart_revenue') }, grid: { drawOnChartArea: false } }
                        }
                    }
                },
                scoreChart: {
                    type: 'bar',
                    data: {
                        labels: [],
                        datasets: [{
                            label: this._t('chart_score'),
                            data: [],
                            backgroundColor: ['rgba(243,156,18,0.7)', 'rgba(142,68,173,0.7)', 'rgba(39,174,96,0.7)'],
                            borderColor: ['#f39c12', '#8e44ad', '#27ae60'],
                            borderWidth: 2
                        }]
                    },
                    options: {
                        responsive: true,
                        maintainAspectRatio: false,
                        plugins: {
                            title: { display: true, text: this._t('chart_score_title') }
                        },
                        scales: {
                            y: { beginAtZero: true, max: 100, title: { display: true, text: this._t('chart_score') } }
                        }
                    }
                }
            };
        }

        getChartData(state) {
            var ds = (state && state.domainState) || {};
            var mh = ds.marginHistory || [], rh = ds.revenueHistory || [], sh = ds.scoreHistory || [];
            var labels = mh.map(function (_, i) { return 'R' + (i + 1); });
            this._paintChartAlt(ds);
            return {
                marginChart: { labels: labels, datasets: [{ data: mh }, { data: rh }] },
                scoreChart: { labels: labels, datasets: [{ data: sh }] }
            };
        }

        // Text alternative for both charts (F14, F21): the same series as a sentence
        _paintChartAlt(ds) {
            var c1 = document.getElementById('marginChart'), c2 = document.getElementById('scoreChart');
            if (c1) c1.setAttribute('aria-label', this._t('chart_fin_title'));
            if (c2) c2.setAttribute('aria-label', this._t('chart_score_title'));
            var el = document.getElementById('costdecChartAlt');
            if (!el) return;
            var mh = ds.marginHistory || [], sh = ds.scoreHistory || [], self = this;
            if (!mh.length) { el.textContent = ''; return; }
            el.textContent = mh.map(function (m, i) {
                return self._tf('chart_alt_row', { r: i + 1, m: self._fmt(m, 1), s: sh[i] });
            }).join(' · ');
        }

        getPerformanceSummary(history) {
            if (!history || !history.length) return {};
            var ds = (window.mySimulation && window.mySimulation.state && window.mySimulation.state.domainState) || {};
            if (!ds.dec) {
                ds = { dec: {}, _rolls: {} };
                for (var h = 0; h < history.length; h++) {
                    var hd = history[h].decisions || {};
                    var rr = history[h].period || (h + 1);
                    ds.dec[String(rr)] = hd;
                    var hds = history[h].domainState || (history[h].results && history[h].results.domainState);
                    if (hds && hds._rolls) ds._rolls = hds._rolls;
                }
            }
            var last = history[history.length - 1].results || {};
            var r = Math.min(3, last.period || history.length);
            var e = this._econ(ds, r);
            var ex = this._econ(ds, r, null, true);
            var sc = this._scores(ds, r, ex);
            var tier = this._tier(sc.overall);
            var diag = this._diagnose(ds, r, ex);
            var insights = diag.items.slice(0, 4).map(function (x) { return x.text; });
            var pos = this._positives(ds, r);
            for (var i = 0; i < pos.length && insights.length < 4; i++) insights.push(pos[i]);
            if (insights.length < 3) insights.push(this._t('ins_generic_close'));
            return {
                totalPeriods: history.length,
                score: sc.overall,
                overallScore: sc.overall,
                totalScore: sc.overall,
                composite: sc.overall,
                outcomeScore: sc.outcome,
                processScore: sc.process,
                performance: tier,
                performanceKey: tier,
                performanceLabel: this._t('tier_' + tier),
                finalMargin: Math.round(10000 * e.profit / e.revenue) / 100,
                finalRevenue: Math.round(e.revenue),
                finalProfit: Math.round(e.profit),
                turningPoint: diag.turning,
                insights: insights,
                questions: [this._t('q1'), this._t('q2'), this._t('q3')]
            };
        }

        // Each decision that differs from the strongest alternative, with its cost in M COP per year, worst first
        _diagnose(ds, r, e) {
            var self = this, D = ds.dec || {}, d1 = D['1'] || {}, d2 = D['2'] || {}, d3 = D['3'] || {};
            var items = [];
            var cost = function (round, key, value) {
                if (round > r) return 0;
                return Math.max(0, self._econ(ds, r, { round: round, key: key, value: value }, true).profit - e.profit);
            };
            var push = function (round, labelKey, textKey, c, extra) {
                var v = Object.assign({ x: self._fmt(c, 0) }, extra || {});
                items.push({ round: round, label: self._t(labelKey), cost: c, text: self._tf(textKey, v) });
            };
            var M = this.MODEL;
            if (d1.ssStrategy === 'drop') push(1, 'ss_strategy_label', 'ins_drop', cost(1, 'ssStrategy', 'reprice'), { s: self._fmt(M.ssUnits * M.ssStrandedUnit, 0) });
            else if (d1.ssStrategy === 'outsource') push(1, 'ss_strategy_label', 'ins_ss_outsource', cost(1, 'ssStrategy', 'reprice'));
            else if (d1.ssStrategy === 'maintain') push(1, 'ss_strategy_label', 'ins_ss_maintain', cost(1, 'ssStrategy', 'reprice'));
            if (d1.paPricing === 'plus18') push(1, 'pa_pricing_label', 'ins_pa_plus18', cost(1, 'paPricing', 'plus10'));
            else if (d1.paPricing === 'maintain') push(1, 'pa_pricing_label', 'ins_pa_maintain', cost(1, 'paPricing', 'plus10'));
            if (d1.capacity === 'idle') push(1, 'capacity_label', 'ins_cap_idle', cost(1, 'capacity', 'expandIC'));
            if (r >= 2 && d1.ssStrategy !== 'drop') {
                if (d2.makeBuy === 'outsource') push(2, 'make_buy_label', 'ins_mb_outsource', cost(2, 'makeBuy', 'make'));
                else if (d2.makeBuy === 'partial') push(2, 'make_buy_label', 'ins_mb_partial', cost(2, 'makeBuy', 'make'));
            }
            if (r >= 2) {
                var vp = +d2.variancePrice || 0, ve = +d2.varianceEff || 0, vv = +d2.varianceVol || 0;
                var err = Math.abs(vp - 3.36) + Math.abs(ve - 6.84) + Math.abs(vv - 5.20);
                var vc = Math.max(0, this._econ(Object.assign({}, ds, { dec: Object.assign({}, D, { '2': Object.assign({}, d2, { variancePrice: 3.36, varianceEff: 6.84, varianceVol: 5.20 }) }) }), r, null, true).profit - e.profit);
                if (vp >= 10) push(2, 'variance_label_short', 'ins_var_price', vc, { p: self._fmt(vp, 2), err: self._fmt(err, 2) });
                else if (ve > 6.84 + 1) push(2, 'variance_label_short', 'ins_var_blame', vc, { e2: self._fmt(ve, 2), err: self._fmt(err, 2) });
                else if (err >= 1) push(2, 'variance_label_short', 'ins_var_off', vc, { err: self._fmt(err, 2) });
                if (d2.transferPrice === 'negotiated') push(2, 'transfer_price_label', 'ins_tp_neg', cost(2, 'transferPrice', 'costPlus'));
                else if (d2.transferPrice === 'market') push(2, 'transfer_price_label', 'ins_tp_market', cost(2, 'transferPrice', 'costPlus'));
            }
            if (r >= 3) {
                if (d3.lease === 'lease') push(3, 'lease_label', 'ins_lease', cost(3, 'lease', 'noLease'));
                if (d3.tocMix === 'statusQuo') push(3, 'toc_mix_label', 'ins_toc_status', cost(3, 'tocMix', 'optimize'));
                else if (d3.tocMix === 'manual') push(3, 'toc_mix_label', 'ins_toc_manual', cost(3, 'tocMix', 'optimize'));
                if (d3.customProduct === 'reject') push(3, 'custom_product_label', 'ins_custom_reject', cost(3, 'customProduct', 'accept'));
            }
            items.sort(function (a, b) { return b.cost - a.cost; });
            var top = items[0];
            var turning = (top && top.cost >= 20)
                ? this._tf('turning_line', { d: top.label, r: top.round, x: this._fmt(top.cost, 0) })
                : this._t('turning_none');
            return { items: items, turning: turning };
        }

        _positives(ds, r) {
            var D = ds.dec || {}, d1 = D['1'] || {}, d2 = D['2'] || {}, d3 = D['3'] || {}, out = [];
            if (d1.ssStrategy === 'reprice') out.push(this._t('pos_reprice'));
            if (r >= 2 && d1.ssStrategy !== 'drop' && d2.makeBuy === 'make') out.push(this._t('pos_make'));
            if (r >= 2) {
                var err = Math.abs((+d2.variancePrice || 0) - 3.36) + Math.abs((+d2.varianceEff || 0) - 6.84) + Math.abs((+d2.varianceVol || 0) - 5.20);
                if (err < 1) out.push(this._t('pos_variance'));
                if (d2.transferPrice === 'costPlus') out.push(this._t('pos_tp_cost'));
            }
            if (r >= 3 && d3.tocMix === 'optimize') out.push(this._t('pos_toc'));
            if (r >= 3 && d3.lease === 'noLease') out.push(this._t('pos_nolease'));
            return out;
        }

        formatCompletionMessage(summary) {
            var s = summary || {}, self = this;
            var esc = function (t) { return String(t === undefined || t === null ? '' : t).replace(/&/g, '&amp;').replace(/</g, '&lt;').replace(/>/g, '&gt;'); };
            var li = function (arr) { return (arr || []).map(function (x) { return '<li>' + esc(x) + '</li>'; }).join(''); };
            var kpi = function (label, value) { return '<div class="costdec-cm-kpi"><span class="costdec-cm-kpi-label">' + esc(label) + '</span><span class="costdec-cm-kpi-value">' + esc(value) + '</span></div>'; };
            return '<div class="costdec-cm" role="region" aria-label="' + esc(this._t('cm_title')) + '">' +
                '<h2 class="costdec-cm-title">' + esc(this._t('cm_title')) + '</h2>' +
                '<p class="costdec-cm-score"><strong>' + esc(s.overallScore) + '/100</strong> · <span class="costdec-cm-tier costdec-cm-tier-' + esc(s.performance) + '">' + esc(s.performanceLabel) + '</span></p>' +
                '<div class="costdec-cm-kpis">' +
                    kpi(this._t('cm_outcome'), (s.outcomeScore === undefined ? '-' : s.outcomeScore) + '/100') +
                    kpi(this._t('cm_process'), (s.processScore === null || s.processScore === undefined ? '-' : s.processScore + '/100')) +
                    kpi(this._t('revenue_label'), this._fmt(s.finalRevenue, 0)) +
                    kpi(this._t('net_margin_label'), this._fmt(s.finalMargin, 1) + '%') +
                    kpi(this._t('profit_label'), this._fmt(s.finalProfit, 0)) +
                '</div>' +
                '<h3 class="costdec-cm-h">' + esc(this._t('cm_turning')) + '</h3><p>' + esc(s.turningPoint) + '</p>' +
                '<h3 class="costdec-cm-h">' + esc(this._t('cm_insights')) + '</h3><ul>' + li(s.insights) + '</ul>' +
                '<h3 class="costdec-cm-h">' + esc(this._t('cm_questions')) + '</h3><ol>' + li(s.questions) + '</ol>' +
                '<p class="costdec-cm-note">' + esc(this._t('cm_note')) + '</p>' +
            '</div>';
        }

        getHint(state, results) {
            if (!results) return null;
            var round = results.period || state.currentPeriod;
            if (round === 1 && results.netMargin < 3) return this._t('hint_r1_low_margin');
            if (round === 2 && results.processScore !== null && results.processScore < 70) return this._t('hint_r2_low_score');
            return null;
